From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: a centred taskbar is centred on the screen

With Settings > Personalization > Taskbar > alignment "Center" (TaskbarAl 1)
the Start button and the window buttons were centred in the room left of the
notification area, the pager and the clock -- so the group sat well left of
the middle of the screen (David: "the start icon is still all the way to the
left"). On Windows the group is centred on the whole bar. Now it is, unless
that would run into the notification area, where it stops beside it.

Gate: test/taskbar-gate.sh (the group's middle is the screen's).
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -1020,7 +1020,15 @@
     if (n && head + n * width > limit)
         width = max( icons ? SG_ICON_BUTTON / 2 : taskbar_button_width / 4, (limit - head) / n );
     total = head + n * width;
-    if (sg_bar.center && total < limit) pos = (limit - total) / 2;
+    /* centred on the whole bar, as on Windows -- not in the room left of
+     * the notification area, which put the group left of the middle --
+     * unless that would run into the notification area */
+    if (sg_bar.center && total < limit)
+    {
+        int full = sg_vertical() ? tray_height : tray_width;
+        pos = (full - total) / 2;
+        if (pos + total > limit) pos = limit - total;
+    }
 
     if (start)
     {
